A note on this license: we haven't decided yet what Nogglebox's final license will be. Until we
do, this is deliberately the most restrictive license we can use: everything is reserved, and
the only permission given is to prepare contributions. That keeps every option open. Because
contributors hand over their rights (section 2), we can move to a different license later,
including a more open one, without having to track down every contributor for permission.

This repository contains the Nogglebox website: its code, pages, videos, recordings, artwork
and text (together, "Nogglebox"). Nogglebox is not open source. Except as stated below, no one
may copy, modify, distribute, publish or otherwise use any part of it without written
permission from the copyright holder.


1. Permission to contribute

You may view this repository, make a copy (including a GitHub fork), and modify that copy, but
only to prepare a contribution to be submitted back to this repository, for example as a pull
request. This permission does not cover publishing, hosting or distributing Nogglebox or any
modified version of it.


2. Contributions

A "contribution" is anything you submit for inclusion in Nogglebox, such as a page, video,
recording, image, text, or code change, whether by pull request or any other means.

By submitting a contribution, you agree that:

 (a) Assignment. You assign to the copyright holder all of your right, title and interest,
     including all copyright, in your contribution, worldwide.

 (b) License, where assignment isn't possible. If any right cannot be assigned under the
     applicable law, you grant the copyright holder an exclusive, perpetual, irrevocable,
     worldwide, royalty-free license to use, copy, modify, publish, distribute, sublicense and
     otherwise exploit your contribution in any way, without credit or payment to you.

 (c) Moral rights. To the fullest extent permitted by law, you waive, and agree not to assert,
     any moral rights in your contribution, including any right to be credited or to object to
     changes.

 (d) Your promises. You promise that:
       - the contribution is your own original work, or you otherwise have the right to make
         this agreement for all of it;
       - it does not infringe anyone else's rights;
       - every identifiable person who appears in it (in video, photos or recordings) has
         agreed to its use on Nogglebox, and for anyone under 18, a parent or legal guardian
         has given that consent;
       - it contains no personal information beyond what those people agreed to share.

 (e) No obligation. The copyright holder may accept, change or reject any contribution, or
     remove it later, at any time and without explanation, and is not required to use it or
     to credit you.


3. Third-party material

Some files in this repository belong to others and are covered by their own licenses, not by
this one. These include the libraries in vendor/ (see vendor/VERSIONS.txt and the notices in
each file), the Baloo 2 font in shared/fonts/ (SIL Open Font License, see shared/fonts/OFL.txt),
and images credited in 8/img/CREDITS.md. Nothing here restricts your rights to those files under
their own licenses.


4. No warranty

Nogglebox is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. The copyright
holder is not liable for any claim, damages or other liability arising from it.
